Subject: [PATCH 18/20] Fix type mismatch in JNI function

SetupControlSocket() returns a boolean value and it's only caller is the
JNI function mainConfigurationSetupControlSocket() that also returns a
boolean value. So, change SetupControlSocket() to boolean.
---
 src/feature/api/org_torproject_jni_TorService.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/feature/api/org_torproject_jni_TorService.c b/src/feature/api/org_torproject_jni_TorService.c
index ff58744258..910248f70e 100644
--- a/src/feature/api/org_torproject_jni_TorService.c
+++ b/src/feature/api/org_torproject_jni_TorService.c
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ SetCommandLine(JNIEnv *env, jobject thisObj, jobjectArray arrArgv)
   return true;
 }
 
-static int
+static bool
 SetupControlSocket(JNIEnv *env, jobject thisObj)
 {
   jclass torApiClass = (*env)->GetObjectClass(env, thisObj);
-- 
2.47.3

